@startuml extension-lifecycle

title Boat Rudder - Extension states (ExtensionState)

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1565C0
}

[*] --> Invalid : manifest fails a check\n(name, title, version, protocol,\nexec, socket path, nav)
[*] --> Disabled : manifest OK,\nno "enabled" document

Invalid : can't be enabled;\nthe admin page shows why
Disabled : no process
Starting : process launched,\nsocket not answering yet
Running : socket answers;\nrequests are forwarded
Failed : 5 exits within 60 s,\nor fork() failed

Invalid --> Disabled : manifest fixed\n(next rescan)
Disabled --> Starting : admin enables\n(supervisor launches it)
Starting --> Running : socket answers
Running --> Starting : process exited\n(restart after 1 s, 2 s, ...)
Starting --> Failed : 5th exit\nwithin 60 s
Failed --> Disabled : admin disables
Failed --> Starting : admin enables again\n(counters reset)
Running --> Disabled : admin disables\n(SIGTERM, SIGKILL after 3 s)
Starting --> Disabled : admin disables
Running --> [*] : server stops\n(SIGTERM to every extension)

note right of Running
  Every second the supervisor checks
  each enabled extension: process alive
  (kill(pid, 0)) and socket answering.
  The "enabled" choice is stored in the
  `extensions` collection and survives
  restarts.
end note

@enduml
